===Defeat the IPC's armed forces{{subst:void|<!--202200306-->}}===
{{Dialogue Start}}
:{{tx}}
:'''???:''' Allow me to introduce myself. I'm Lingsha, Cauldron Master and Head of the Alchemy Commission on the Luofu.
:'''Dan Heng:''' Could she be...?
:'''Yanqing:''' Yeah, she's the new Cauldron Master assigned here from the Xianzhou Zhuming.
:'''Lingsha:''' I received a report from the Artisanship Commission about cargo containing samples of unknown organisms. It said they needed help from the Alchemy Commission. I had nothing better to do, so I came myself.
:'''Lingsha:''' It's fine, Mr. Skott. If you really don't want your cargo to be inspected, it doesn't matter.
:'''Yanqing:''' It doesn't matter? How can you say that?
:'''Skott:''' Why are you being so nice all of a sudden? Well, since you're not going to check it, I'll take this crate and be on my way. Is that okay with everyone?
:'''Lingsha:''' Yeah, sure. Why should I object? Not only this sample, but all the goods on the transport ship are yours to keep. Like I said, we won't inspect them.
:'''Yanqing:''' Wait a minute!
:'''Skott:''' Well, that's more like it! If only the young displayed a more... reasonable attitude, we could have sidestepped that altercation just now.
:'''Skott:''' Our ship will leave in a few days once the engines are repaired.
:'''Lingsha:''' Your ship can leave whenever you want, but I'm afraid I can't say the same for the cargo.
:'''Lingsha:''' According to the import and export regulations signed between the Xianzhou and IPC, all biological shipments can only leave the port when they have confirmed to be of no threat, or when all biological activity expires.
:'''Lingsha:''' Since we can't determine if your shipment is safe for the environment, I guess we'll have to wait for its biological activity to expire. Let me check the previous cases...
:'''Lingsha:''' Normally it'll only take around forty-seven star calendar years.
:'''Skott:''' "Only" forty-seven years?
:'''Lingsha:''' Why so surprised? You're still young and full of energy. I'm pretty sure you'll live a few more decades. Have some confidence in yourself!
:'''Skott:''' Typical of a long-life species, your words are dripping with sarcasm. While you may not care about time, I do! I'll be demanding double compensation from the Sky-Faring Commission for every minute wasted!
:'''Lingsha:''' Sure thing, Mr. Skott. You seem pretty confident that your career and life will last long enough to witness this victory unfold.
:'''Skott:''' ...
:'''Skott:''' Step aside, guys. Let them do the inspection.
:'''IPC Worker:''' But Mr. Skott...
:'''Skott:''' Come on, we're already in enough trouble... Just let them do the security inspection. And if needed, I can always grovel before the Intelligentsia Guild later &mdash; I'm just using my head for what it's apparently good for, right?
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Sorry for the trouble.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Thanks, bro.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} At least you've wised up for once.
:'''Skott:''' Well, honestly, at least you're not as annoying as that woman.
:'''Skott:''' Just get on with the inspection! Don't act all chummy with me now that you've got your way.
:'''March 7th:''' This lady... is really something else!
:{{tx}}
{{Dialogue End}}

